ames>JN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Behavioral phenotyping of transgenic and knockout mice: experimental design and evaluation of general health, sensory functions, motor abilities, and specific behavioral tests</article-title><source><italic>Brain Research</italic></source><year>1999</year><volume>835</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10448192</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MGI</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Mouse Genome Informatics</article-title><year>2006</year><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.informatics.jax.org/">http://www.informatics.jax.org/</ext-link>.</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MPD</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Mouse Phenome Database</article-title><year>2006</year><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://phenome.jax.org/pub-cgi/phenome/mpdcgi">http://phenome.jax.org/pub-cgi/phenome/mpdcgi</ext-link>.</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Singewald</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Salchner</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharp</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Induction of c-Fos expression in specific areas of the fear circuitry in rat forebrain by anxiogenic drugs</article-title><source><italic>Biological Psychiatry</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>53</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>275</fpage><lpage>283</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12586446</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dagnino-Subiabre</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Orellana</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Carmona-Fontaine</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Chronic stress decreases the expression of sympathetic markers in the pineal gland and increases plasma melatonin concentration in rats</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Neurochemistry</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>97</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>1279</fpage><lpage>1287</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16539651</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kalueff</surname><given-names>AV</given-names></name><name><surname>Nutt</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of GABA in memory and anxiety</article-title><source><italic>Depression and Anxiety</italic></source><year>1996</year><volume>4</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>100</fpage><lpage>110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9166638</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wall</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Messier</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Concurrent modulation of anxiety and memory</article-title><source><italic>Behavioural Brain Research</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>109</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>229</fpage><lpage>241</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10762693</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yerkes</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Dodson</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The relation of strength of stimulus to rapidity of habit-formation</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Comparative Neurology and Psychology</italic></source><year>1908</year><volume>18</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>459</fpage><lpage>482</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barad</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fear extinction in rodents: basic insight to clinical promise</article-title><source><italic>Current Opinion in Neurobiology</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>15</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>710</fpage><lpage>715</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16260129</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beuzen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Belzung</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Link between emotional memory and anxiety states: a study by principal component analysis</article-title><source><italic>Physiology and Behavior</italic></source><year>1995</year><volume>58</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>118</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7667407</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chapouthier</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Venault</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>GABAA receptor complex and memory processes</article-title><source><italic>Medicinal Chemistry Reviews</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>1</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>99</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gerlai</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Memory enhancement: the progress and our fears</article-title><source><italic>Genes, Brain and Behavior</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>2</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>190</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parent</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Habib</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Time-dependent changes in brain monoamine oxidase activity and in brain levels of monoamines and amino acids following acute administration of the antidepressant/antipanic drug phenelzine</article-title><source><italic>Biochemical Pharmacology</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>59</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>1253</fpage><lpage>1263</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10736426</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Quirk</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gehlert</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inhibition of the amygdala: key to pathological states?</article-title><source><italic>Annals of the New York Academy of Sciences</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>985</volume><fpage>263</fpage><lpage>272</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12724164</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Izquierdo</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Medina</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>GABAA receptor modulation of memory: the role of endogenous benzodiazepines</article-title><source><italic>Trends in Pharmacological Sciences</italic></source><year>1991</year><volume>12</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>260</fpage><lpage>265</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1658996</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Izquierdo</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Medina</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Correlation between the pharmacology of long-term potentiation and the pharmacology of memory</article-title><source><italic>Neurobiology of Learning and Memory</italic></source><year>1995</year><volume>63</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7663877</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bannerman</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Rawlins</surname><given-names>JNP</given-names></name><name><surname>McHugh</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Regional dissociations within the hippocampus&#x02014;memory and anxiety</article-title><source><italic>Neuroscience and Biobehavioral Reviews</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>28</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>273</fpage><lpage>283</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15225971</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B24"><label>24</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bierman</surname><given-names>EJM</given-names></name><name><surname>Comijs</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Jonker</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Beekman</surna